WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.934 --> 00:00:02.334
-Sean, thank you for being here.

00:00:02.334 --> 00:00:04.503
How's everything with the show?
I'm very excited.

00:00:04.503 --> 00:00:05.805
That's February 18th?

00:00:05.805 --> 00:00:07.707
-February 18th, the game show,
and then "Hot Ones"

00:00:07.707 --> 00:00:10.743
on First We Feast's YouTube
starts right back up next week.

00:00:10.743 --> 00:00:12.912
-Next week.
-Margot Robbie for the premiere.

00:00:12.912 --> 00:00:14.614
Yeah.
-Oh, my gosh. Alright, alright.

00:00:14.614 --> 00:00:15.815
Here we go.
-Sean, I'm starving. Let's go.

00:00:15.815 --> 00:00:17.383
-Thank you for doing this.

00:00:17.383 --> 00:00:18.718
-Thanks so much for
having me, Jimmy.

00:00:18.718 --> 00:00:20.086
Thanks for having me back.

00:00:20.086 --> 00:00:22.321
J.J., it's an honor to have you
here in the hot seat.

00:00:22.321 --> 00:00:25.324
And for those of you who are
wondering what the hell

00:00:25.324 --> 00:00:28.260
is going on right here,
"Hot Ones" is simple.

00:00:28.260 --> 00:00:30.497
We interview celebrities while
eating increasingly spicy

00:00:30.497 --> 00:00:33.199
chicken wings,
and, as Jimmy can attest,

00:00:33.199 --> 00:00:36.703
it gets very spicy very
quickly on "The Tonight Show."

00:00:36.703 --> 00:00:38.971
We'll start in a mild zone
and work our way up to

00:00:38.971 --> 00:00:41.474
the Last Dab XXX,
a sauce more than

00:00:41.474 --> 00:00:44.210
250 times hotter than
a jalapeño.

00:00:44.210 --> 00:00:46.579
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:46.579 --> 00:00:49.782
The line is always hits
on live TV.

00:00:49.782 --> 00:00:52.785
-It is all fun now.
Get ready, dude. It's insane.

00:00:52.785 --> 00:00:54.119
-Alright.
-Alright.

00:00:54.119 --> 00:00:56.355
-So, we'll start at the handle,
Los Calientes Rojo,

00:00:56.355 --> 00:00:59.125
a turning-point sauce,
our halfway sauce.

00:00:59.125 --> 00:01:00.593
-Okay. Alright.
-Here we go.

00:01:00.593 --> 00:01:02.328
-Just eat the whole thing? Yeah?

00:01:02.328 --> 00:01:05.098
-Up to you.
-Okay.

00:01:05.098 --> 00:01:06.832
-Alright.

00:01:06.832 --> 00:01:08.034
-Tasty.
-Yeah, not bad.

00:01:08.034 --> 00:01:10.069
-Smoky.
-Delightful.

00:01:10.069 --> 00:01:11.237
-Alright, J.J.,
my first question is for you.

00:01:11.237 --> 00:01:12.772
-Okay.

00:01:12.772 --> 00:01:15.475
-I know when you were a walk-on
at the University of Wisconsin,

00:01:15.475 --> 00:01:19.445
to make ends meet, you were
a deliver driver for Pizza Hut.

00:01:19.445 --> 00:01:22.414
What can you tell people about
that ill-fated day

00:01:22.414 --> 00:01:25.685
where you were forced to eat
a customer's hot wings.

00:01:25.685 --> 00:01:29.522
-This is true, actually.
So -- Sorry.

00:01:29.522 --> 00:01:31.291
I was a pizza delivery driver,

00:01:31.291 --> 00:01:32.625
and it was a snowy day
in Wisconsin.

00:01:32.625 --> 00:01:34.093
They closed schools.
They closed businesses.

00:01:34.093 --> 00:01:35.428
They closed everything.

00:01:35.428 --> 00:01:37.397
Pizza Hut was
considering closing.

00:01:37.397 --> 00:01:39.699
I told them,
"No, my parents have a truck."

00:01:39.699 --> 00:01:41.334
So I can drive in the snow."

00:01:41.334 --> 00:01:45.038
I came in, took an order out,
spun out into a mailbox,

00:01:45.038 --> 00:01:48.274
wiped out a mailbox,
ended up in the front yard.

00:01:48.274 --> 00:01:51.677
Called a tow truck.
A little spicy, not too spicy.

00:01:51.677 --> 00:01:52.745
A little bit of spice.

00:01:52.745 --> 00:01:54.480
-I was gonna say,
get into the story --

00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:55.614
Yeah, yeah.

00:01:55.614 --> 00:01:58.250
-So, I call a tow truck.
Tow truck spins out.

00:01:58.250 --> 00:01:59.419
It's gone.

00:01:59.419 --> 00:02:00.953
So I'm sitting in a car
with nothing to do

00:02:00.953 --> 00:02:03.089
but two pizzas
and hot wings on the --

00:02:03.089 --> 00:02:04.257
I ate the hot wings.

00:02:04.257 --> 00:02:06.392
-Football players got to eat.
They got to eat.

00:02:06.392 --> 00:02:09.095
You don't have to apologize
for that, J.J.

00:02:09.095 --> 00:02:11.798
And as we move on here,
the good news is --

00:02:11.798 --> 00:02:13.299
we're only going for four wings.

00:02:13.299 --> 00:02:16.803
The bad news --
very steep ramp up.

00:02:16.803 --> 00:02:17.804
-Okay.

00:02:17.804 --> 00:02:19.839
-This is a Hot Thai Green
Hot Sauce.

00:02:19.839 --> 00:02:23.609
-Thai green?
-Thai?

00:02:23.609 --> 00:02:25.478
-Oh, man, this is kind of
ramping up, right?

00:02:25.478 --> 00:02:28.080
-Mm-hmm.

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:31.684
-Okay.
-Alright.

00:02:31.684 --> 00:02:35.154
-Okay.
-Jimmy on top of it.

00:02:35.154 --> 00:02:38.091
I understand, Jimmy,
that you did not have

00:02:38.091 --> 00:02:39.691
the most athletic childhood,

00:02:39.691 --> 00:02:41.895
but it wasn't for
lack of trying.

00:02:41.895 --> 00:02:44.363
I know it wasn't for
lack of trying.

00:02:44.363 --> 00:02:46.732
What can you tell us about
your dad installing

00:02:46.732 --> 00:02:49.401
a basketball hoop
for you when were a kid?

00:02:49.401 --> 00:02:52.071
-I got a basketball hoop
for Christmas from Santa Claus,

00:02:52.071 --> 00:02:53.940
and my dad didn't want to
put it on the garage

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:56.442
because he thought the garage
would fall down.

00:02:56.442 --> 00:02:58.911
And so he put it in
the middle of our backyard,

00:02:58.911 --> 00:03:01.147
in the grass, in the lawn.

00:03:01.147 --> 00:03:04.016
You can't dribble a ball
on grass.

00:03:04.016 --> 00:03:06.152
And my dad was like, "Well, you
can just do foul shots."

00:03:06.152 --> 00:03:07.386
And I go, "No.

00:03:07.386 --> 00:03:08.787
No one is going to come over
and play with me,"

00:03:08.787 --> 00:03:13.559
and so I hadn't had a
friend ever since.

00:03:13.559 --> 00:03:15.161
-Moving -- You have a friend
in me, Jimmy.

00:03:15.161 --> 00:03:17.030
-Thank you.
-You have two friends.

00:03:17.030 --> 00:03:19.699
-Moving on.
Well, at least for now.

00:03:19.699 --> 00:03:21.167
We'll see about
the friendship after this.

00:03:21.167 --> 00:03:22.501
-Oh, no. This is not it.

00:03:22.501 --> 00:03:25.671
-This is
Da Bomb Beyond Insanity,

00:03:25.671 --> 00:03:26.738
a sauce we have to
apologize for.

00:03:26.738 --> 00:03:27.773
-You have experience?

00:03:27.773 --> 00:03:29.976
-So, J.J., in advance,
I say I'm sorry.

00:03:29.976 --> 00:03:33.112
Jimmy, you know the drill
with this one.

00:03:33.112 --> 00:03:34.613
-J.J., this is honestly
the turning point.

00:03:34.613 --> 00:03:35.948
-It's only number three.

00:03:35.948 --> 00:03:39.385
-No, this really -- This hurts
my feelings, this one.

00:03:39.385 --> 00:03:40.619
This one insults me.

00:03:40.619 --> 00:03:41.921
-I feel like it could hurt
something else, too,

00:03:41.921 --> 00:03:43.355
the way you're talking about it.

00:03:43.355 --> 00:03:44.657
-It's bad news. Alright.

00:03:44.657 --> 00:03:48.194
-Alright, let's dig in.
-Oh, my gosh.

00:03:48.194 --> 00:03:50.195
-Okay, yep.

00:03:50.195 --> 00:03:52.699
-Immediate?
-Yep.

00:03:57.403 --> 00:03:59.439
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:03.743 --> 00:04:06.445
-Yeah.

00:04:06.445 --> 00:04:10.049
-It's almost like poison.
-Yeah, that's not pleasant.

00:04:10.049 --> 00:04:11.583
The taste isn't even pleasant.
It's not pleasant.

00:04:11.583 --> 00:04:12.785
-No.
-No.

00:04:12.785 --> 00:04:14.820
-Very few redeeming qualities
with this one.

00:04:14.820 --> 00:04:17.389
-No. I don't like it.
I don't like it.

00:04:17.389 --> 00:04:19.992
-On the topic of J.J.
hosting "SNL" this weekend --

00:04:19.992 --> 00:04:22.295
-Screw "SNL."

00:04:22.295 --> 00:04:25.297
I mean, I...

00:04:25.297 --> 00:04:27.032
I love "SNL." I'm hosting it.

00:04:27.032 --> 00:04:29.635
You should probably --
Jesus, man!

00:04:29.635 --> 00:04:30.936
-It's the sauce talking.

00:04:30.936 --> 00:04:34.139
Jimmy, who do you think is
the funniest athlete

00:04:34.139 --> 00:04:35.307
to ever host the show?

00:04:35.307 --> 00:04:36.509
-Everyone, everyone.
-Dude...

00:04:36.509 --> 00:04:39.445
-And what advice, if any,
do you have for J.J.?

00:04:39.445 --> 00:04:42.548
-Read the cards.
-I need advice for this, Jimmy.

00:04:42.548 --> 00:04:47.220
-Do the sketch.
-The air hurts.

00:04:47.220 --> 00:04:49.722
-Well, then --
-Stop talking so loud.

00:04:49.722 --> 00:04:55.060
-It is a good thing that we're
approaching the end of the line.

00:04:55.060 --> 00:04:56.729
This is the Last Dab.

00:04:56.729 --> 00:04:58.965
Let's make some noise
for Jimmy and J.J.

00:04:58.965 --> 00:05:02.234
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:02.234 --> 00:05:04.270
A heroic run.

00:05:04.270 --> 00:05:06.338
We call it the Last Dab
because it is tradition

00:05:06.338 --> 00:05:10.509
around here to put a
little extra on the last one.

00:05:10.509 --> 00:05:12.378
You don't have to.
-You do what?

00:05:12.378 --> 00:05:13.846
-You dab the last wing, but
you don't have to --

00:05:13.846 --> 00:05:15.114
-With what? That?
-Yep.

00:05:15.114 --> 00:05:18.818
-That's hotter than that?
Are you nuts?

00:05:18.818 --> 00:05:24.756
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:24.756 --> 00:05:30.529
[ Audience groans ]
Oh!

00:05:30.529 --> 00:05:33.499
-Alright, yeah.

00:05:33.499 --> 00:05:34.534
[ Groans ]

00:05:34.534 --> 00:05:37.470
-Alright.

00:05:37.470 --> 00:05:39.505
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:48.647 --> 00:05:51.850
-They're getting on their feet,
and that means

00:05:51.850 --> 00:05:54.420
that we have reached
the end of the gauntlet,

00:05:54.420 --> 00:05:56.956
approaching the finish line,
and, Jimmy,

00:05:56.956 --> 00:05:59.358
it's become a tradition
here on "The Tonight Show"

00:05:59.358 --> 00:06:00.726
for us to play a little game.

00:06:00.726 --> 00:06:02.495
And there is so much --
-Alright, what's the rules --

00:06:02.495 --> 00:06:03.929
-Nope, I'm done!

00:06:03.929 --> 00:06:07.065
-So much anticipation for
this weekend's Super Bowl

00:06:07.065 --> 00:06:08.934
and, of course, the halftime
performance with

00:06:08.934 --> 00:06:10.836
J.Lo and Shakira.

00:06:10.836 --> 00:06:16.576
So, with your brain on fire,
tongue ablaze, mouth an inferno,

00:06:16.576 --> 00:06:17.876
can you try to do
an impression --

00:06:17.876 --> 00:06:19.812
-I don't want
to play any games, Sean!

00:06:19.812 --> 00:06:22.214
-Can you do an impression of
a Super Bowl

00:06:22.214 --> 00:06:23.716
performer from years past?

00:06:23.716 --> 00:06:26.652
J.J., it's up to you to try
to guess the impression.

00:06:26.652 --> 00:06:29.088
-Is this a prop?
-No, that's straight milk.

00:06:29.088 --> 00:06:30.089
Go ahead.
-No, no.

00:06:30.089 --> 00:06:31.390
-I won't, I won't, I won't,
I won't.

00:06:31.390 --> 00:06:33.659
-If you drink milk --
-When you breathe, it hurts.

00:06:33.659 --> 00:06:36.328
-Yeah. What was the question?
What was the question?

00:06:36.328 --> 00:06:40.066
-An impression of a performer
from Super Bowls past.

00:06:40.066 --> 00:06:41.300
-Okay.

00:06:41.300 --> 00:06:42.301
-Who?

00:06:42.301 --> 00:06:44.303
[ Singing indistinctly ]

00:06:44.303 --> 00:06:45.805
-Mick Jagger!
-Yeah, yeah, perfect.

00:06:45.805 --> 00:06:48.674
-Spot-on Mick Jagger.
Let's make some noise...

00:06:48.674 --> 00:06:49.941
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Water?

00:06:49.941 --> 00:06:54.213
-...for Jimmy and J.J.

00:06:54.213 --> 00:06:55.281
-Cheers, buddy.
-Cheers.

00:06:55.281 --> 00:06:56.882
-Thanks to J.J. Watt
and Sean Evans.

00:06:56.882 --> 00:06:58.717
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:58.717 --> 00:07:00.552
You guys,
Season 11 of "Hot Ones"

00:07:00.552 --> 00:07:02.288
